  "description_short": "Relaxed pub in Storms River serving hearty meals, cold drinks, and warm hospitality after adventure.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into the heart of Storms River village, Hunters Pub is the kind of unpretentious watering hole where hikers, bikers, and locals gather after a day exploring Tsitsikamma. The atmosphere is laid-back and welcoming, with wooden tables, a well-stocked bar, and that easy camaraderie you find in small-town pubs.\n\nThe menu leans into satisfying pub classics—think generous burgers, steaks, and seafood platters that hit the spot when you've worked up an appetite on the trails. Portions are decent, prices are fair, and the beer is reliably cold. It's not fancy, but it doesn't pretend to be.\n\nWhat makes Hunters Pub worth the stop is its role as a village gathering place. It's where adventure stories get swapped, travel tips are shared, and you can feel the pulse of this gateway town to one of South Africa's most dramatic coastlines. A proper local spot in every sense.",
